From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:54:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] voice_input: dictate into the agent composer, transcribed on
 this machine

Typing a long instruction to the agent is often slower than saying it.
This adds a microphone to the agent composer: the speech is turned
into text on this machine by whisper.cpp and put into the composer
unsent, to be read and fixed before it is sent. Story 044.

What it adds:

  * crate voice_input: the `voice_input` settings section, the pinned
    model table, the model download, microphone capture (cpal on its
    own thread, the device chosen by the audio crate's input setting;
    F32, I16, U16, I24 and I32 inputs, 120 s at most), resampling to
    16 kHz mono with rodio, local (whisper-rs) and remote
    transcription, and a pure state machine (state.rs) that decides
    what a click, a key press and a key release mean. One app-wide
    VoiceInput entity runs its effects. Inputs and events carry the
    composer's entity id, so one recording runs at a time; another
    composer is told "Voice input is busy in another thread".
  * agent_ui: a mic button beside Send (m:ss while recording, a
    spinner while transcribing, disabled when read-only), a strip
    above the editor for the download consent and its progress, and
    MessageEditor::insert_transcript: it replaces the newest selection
    as one undo step, adds a space when the char before the
    selection's start is not whitespace, and never sends. A transcript
    for a closed thread is discarded with a toast; one refused by a
    read-only composer is logged outcome=refused.
  * Keys, in all four default keymaps (vim.json included):
    voice_input::ToggleRecording on ctrl-alt-v (cmd-alt-v on macOS). A
    tap (< 300 ms) toggles, a hold is push-to-talk until the key or its
    modifiers are released, and the command palette's toggle is always
    a tap. Escape cancels a recording or declines the consent, except
    while a completion menu is open, which it closes first.
  * reqwest_client: ReqwestClient::without_proxy, which zed/main.rs
    hands to voice_input for plain-http loopback URLs.
  * zlog: whisper_rs is filtered at warn (it logs model details at info
    on every load).

Why a patch: an extension can neither record audio nor add a button
to the composer. Why these two crates: nothing in the tree turns
speech into text. whisper-rs 0.16.0 (Unlicense) is a safe API over
whisper.cpp; whisper-rs-sys 0.15.0 (Unlicense) builds whisper.cpp
1.8.3 (MIT) through CMake from its bundled source. Both were the
newest on crates.io on 2026-10-18, published 2026-03-12. They are the
only third-party crates Cargo.lock gains, beside voice_input itself.
Resampling (rodio), capture (cpal) and hashing (sha2) use crates
already locked; the WAV for the remote service is 44 bytes by hand.

The model: /usr/share/whisper-models (app-accessibility/whisper-models)
first, its size checked on every use and its SHA-256 once per path and
mtime; else <data_dir>/voice/models. A missing model is downloaded
only after a click on Download in the consent strip, from Hugging Face
ggerganov/whisper.cpp at commit 5359861c739e955e79d9a303bcbc70fb988958b1:

  https://huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp/resolve/<commit>/ggml-<model>.bin
  tiny   77691713 B  be07e048e1e599ad46341c8d2a135645097a538221678b7acdd1b1919c6e1b21
  base  147951465 B  60ed5bc3dd14eea856493d334349b405782ddcaf0028d4b5df4088345fba2efe
  small 487601967 B  1be3a9b2063867b937e64e2ec7483364a79917e157fa98c5d94b5c1fffea987b

It is written to a .download-* file in the same directory, held under
an exclusive lock, and renamed into place only with the pinned size
and SHA-256. A cancel, a 30 s stall, an oversized body or a wrong
digest leaves nothing at the final path. A download outlives the
composer that asked for it, and the next composer adopts its strip.
Stale .download-* files (older than 60 s, held by no running Zeo) are
swept at start. A downloaded model whisper cannot load is deleted, to
be downloaded again; a packaged one is left alone.

Privacy: local mode opens no connection; the model download, after
consent, is the only network use. The remote service is off by default
(voice_input.remote.enabled: false). When it is on, the recording goes
as a 16 kHz mono WAV to the OpenAI-compatible endpoint in
voice_input.remote.url: https, or plain http to a loopback host, sent
direct past any proxy. The mic button's tooltip names the host. The
API key is read per request from the environment variable that
voice_input.remote.api_key_env names (default ZEO_VOICE_API_KEY), sent
only as a bearer token, never written to settings and never logged.
Neither mode falls back to the other. Logs are key=value lines
("voice_input event=recording mode= audio_ms= backend= model=
transcribe_ms= outcome=", event=model_download, ...) with no
transcript, audio, key, or URL user-info and query.

Settings ("voice_input" in settings.json): enabled (true), model
("base"; "tiny" or "small"), language ("auto" or a two-letter code),
remote { enabled (false), url (null), model ("whisper-1"),
api_key_env ("ZEO_VOICE_API_KEY") }. "enabled": false hides the button
and leaves the shortcut unbound.

Packaging: USE voice (default on) in app-editors/zeo, its own series
group after every devtools group and epic, and before test. Generated
on top of the claude-agent-acp-plus group, whose composer hunks
(0043-0045) it sits beside, so REQUIRED_USE ties voice? to it. It
needs none of the optional groups: it applies with no fuzz with
claude-code-ide, devtools-bridge, ai-jail, browser-extension,
devtools-panel and epic each on or off (eleven combinations checked),
the zed crate and the voice tests build with only the acp-plus group
under them, and 0050/0051 apply on top of it unchanged. The ebuild
adds whisper-rs@0.16.0 and whisper-rs-sys@0.15.0 to CRATES, LICENSE
voice? ( Unlicense ), and exports GGML_NATIVE=OFF and
WHISPER_DONT_GENERATE_BINDINGS=1 (with ggml's own x86 flags off), so
whisper.cpp follows CFLAGS and builds from its bundled bindings.

Tests: cargo test -p voice_input (204: state machine, transcript,
audio, models, settings, download, capture, local and remote,
entity), cargo test -p agent_ui voice (64), cargo test -p
reqwest_client without_proxy.
