+// Story 044, task 8.5 (refine v3) — a model download outlives the composer that asked for it
+// (R5.1, R6.3, R6.6, R6.14, R6.15; design.md C1.9 `AdoptDownload`, C1.10 abandonment). Wired in
+// the crate root `src/voice_input.rs` as
+//
+//     #[cfg(test)]
+//     mod download_owner_tests;
+//
+// Validation filter: `download_owner` (every test path is `download_owner_tests::…`).
+//
+// Contract: `state::Input::AdoptDownload { owner }` — in `Downloading` the owner becomes `owner`
+// and the effect is `Render`; in every other phase nothing happens. The entity keeps a running
+// download when its composer closes: the next composer's start input adopts it (it then sees the
+// progress and the Cancel control, and is not told busy) and is consumed; `DownloadCancel` still
+// cancels it, and so does turning the feature off. A download that ends after its owner closed
+// notifies nobody.
+//
+// The download is served by a body the test feeds by hand, so "still running" is observable: the
+// body reader is never dropped, it keeps being read, and the staging file keeps growing.
+//
+// Gap: "it completes, with the model at the final path" cannot be driven — a model is only kept
+// when its bytes hash to the pinned SHA-256, which a test cannot produce for a real model. The
+// test instead lets the download run to the end of its body (a short body, so it ends as a
+// checksum mismatch): the body was read to EOF and never dropped early, the staging file is
+// deleted (R6.6) and the phase is Idle.
+//
+// Hostile halves, the wrong collapse first: with A still open, B is refused as busy and A keeps
+// its download (adoption is not a free-for-all); once B adopted it, a third composer C is busy too,
+// and B's own second click changes nothing. Then the wrong split: B, a different composer from the
+// one that consented, does take the download over when A is gone. Then the plain cases.
+
+use std::{
+    collections::VecDeque,
+    path::Path,
+    pin::Pin,
+    sync::{
+        Arc, Mutex,
+        atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering},
+    },
+    task::{Context, Poll, Waker},
+    time::{Duration, Instant},
+};
+
+use futures::AsyncRead;
+use gpui::{AppContext as _, Entity, EntityId, TestAppContext, UpdateGlobal as _};
+use http_client::{AsyncBody, FakeHttpClient, HttpClient, Response};
+use settings::SettingsStore;
+
+use crate::capture::{ActiveCapture, CaptureBackend, CaptureEvent};
